      ⍝ bug-apl@gnu.org, 6/17/2026 (Dave Alden):
      ⍝ A ⎕PLOT B always used ASCII driver if any attribute was provided,
      ⍝ ignoring the compile-time default driver. Explicit ASCII must still work:
      ⊃⍴⍴(⊂'gui_driver: ASCII') ⎕PLOT ⍳5
3

      ⍝ regression (Dave Alden 6/24/2026): LHA with attributes but no gui_driver
      ⍝ must still use the compile-time default — in ASCII builds that means ASCII:
      ⊃⍴⍴(⊂'caption: regression test') ⎕PLOT ⍳5
3

      ⍝ ASCII-plot f(x)=sin(x)÷x in the x range where 10≥|f(x)|
      ⍝ (i.e. all x ≠ 0 with |x|≤10 in steps of 0.1)
      x ← (¯0.1 × ⌽⍳100), 0.1 × ⍳100
      y ← (1○x)÷x
      Z ← ('gui_driver: ASCII' 'terminal_rows: 15' 'terminal_cols: 60') ⎕PLOT (10≥|y)/y
      ⎕←Z[1;;]
